 "explanation": "Tempester Voice, item 5: the release has its own curve (the Voice OS study §6.2, §14.5), attack and decay unchanged. Release index r = clamp(Release - (d_release >> 8), 0, 127), computed by DSI's code up to S (`mov W3,W1`) in each of the five envelopes (pitch, filter, amp, aux 1, aux 2). From S, DSI computes the decrement with bit-by-bit shift loops (R = T[r] >> 7, D = L >> 13, dec = ((D * R) mod 2^32) >> 2, stored at [address], then rom:S+0x6E subtracts it). RELSTEP does the same arithmetic with multi-bit shifts (and stores R and D where DSI did), so for r <= 100 the level is DSI's frame by frame, in fewer cycles than DSI's loops; for r >= 101 it reads F from RELTAB (the rate in 1/256 units) and gives dec = (D * F) >> 10 (D < 2^18, F < 2^11: exact). F comes from the release table generator: t(i) = t(100) * g^(i - 100) up to 60 s at 127, every time distinct and increasing, within 1 % of its target; no index is endless any more. Per envelope: the level address, the call, the jump to S+0x6E.",
